description:
Implement a 3-stage pipeline circuit that sequentially processes a single input signal. The input `in` is captured on the rising edge of the clock and passed through three registers (`reg1`, `reg2`, and `reg3`), with each register storing the value from the previous stage on the next clock edge. Ultimately, the output `out` reflects the value from the third stage, effectively introducing a delay of three clock cycles before the input signal is outputted.
module top_module( 
    input clk,       // Add clk as an input
    input in, 
    output out 
);

code:
module top_module( 
    input clk,       // Add clk as an input
    input in, 
    output out 
);reg reg1, reg2, reg3;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    reg1 <= in;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    reg2 <= reg1;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    reg3 <= reg2;
end

assign out = reg3;

endmodule

