description:
Design a 4-bit binary to Gray code converter. On each rising edge of the clock, the module takes a 4-bit binary input and produces the corresponding 4-bit Gray code output. The conversion is done by directly assigning the least significant bit and using the exclusive OR operation for the other bits, effectively transforming the binary input into its Gray code representation.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    input clk,
    output reg [3:0] out
);always @(posedge clk) begin
    out[0] <= in[0];
    out[1] <= in[0] ^ in[1];
    out[2] <= in[1] ^ in[2];
    out[3] <= in[2] ^ in[3];
end

endmodule

