description:
Create a bus hold block that maintains the last valid value of a signal when the input is in a high-impedance state (Z). The circuit captures the input signal and outputs it directly when it is valid; however, if the input enters a high-impedance state, it will continue to output the last valid signal value, effectively retaining the state of the bus during idle periods.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output reg out
);reg last_valid_value;
  wire tri_state_buffer_output;
  assign tri_state_buffer_output = in;

  always @(*) begin
    if (tri_state_buffer_output === 1'bZ) begin
      out = last_valid_value;
    end
    else begin
      out = tri_state_buffer_output;
      last_valid_value = tri_state_buffer_output;
    end
  end

endmodule

