description:
Design a dual-clock pipeline register system that captures input data on one clock (clk1) and outputs that data on a second clock (clk2). The module includes asynchronous active-low reset signals for both clocks to initialize the registers. When clk1 rises, the input data is stored in an intermediate register, and this stored data is then transferred to the output register on the rising edge of clk2. This design allows for data synchronization between two different clock domains, making it useful for interfacing components operating at different clock frequencies.
